Package: web888-web888d
Architecture: armhf
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, adduser, web888-redpitaya (>= 2025.430-3), web888-websdr (>= 2026.1020-2)
Description: web888d SDR server for Web-888 (RX-888) - Debian build
 From-source build of jeskko/web888-ng v0.6.0 (web888d daemon + web UI),
 statically linked for armhf. Experimental optional third runtime mode
 alongside WebSDR and the Red Pitaya apps: the service ships DISABLED
 (no [Install]) and Conflicts= with web888-websdr.service and all four
 web888-rpapp@ instances, so the FPGA, /dev/zynqsdr and TCP 8073 stay
 exclusive.
 .
 The bitstream is loaded as root by /usr/lib/web888/web888-fpga-select in a
 separate default-off oneshot unit (web888-web888d-pl.service, xdevcfg
 access confined to it); the daemon runs unprivileged (user web888d, group
 web888) with --bitstream none, never touching /dev/xdevcfg. State lives in
 /var/lib/web888d; the mutable config /etc/web888d/web888d.toml is created
 on first install (web888d-owned 0600, not a dpkg conffile). No skimmers,
 no uploads and no admin password by default.
 .
 Depends on web888-redpitaya (runtime switcher and FPGA-select helper) and
 web888-websdr (udev rule, web888 device group and stock firmware floor); an
 open-FPGA bitstream can be provided by web888-ng-bitstream.
